{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1781","published":"2026-03-27T11:10:48Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:45.877100992Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-33412"],"summary":"vim security update","details":"Vim is an advanced text editor that seeks to provide the power of the de-facto Unix editor &amp;apos;Vi&amp;apos;, with a more complete feature set. Vim is a highly configurable text editor built to enable efficient text editing. It is an improved version of the vi editor distributed with most UNIX systems.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to version 9.2.0202, a command injection vulnerability exists in Vim&apos;s glob() function on Unix-like systems. By including a newline character (\\n) in a pattern passed to glob(), an attacker may be able to execute arbitrary shell commands. This vulnerability depends on the user&apos;s &apos;shell&apos; setting. This issue has been patched in version 9.2.0202.(CVE-2026-33412)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"vim","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/vim&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0-41.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["vim-X11-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","vim-common-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","vim-debuginfo-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","vim-debugsource-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","vim-enhanced-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","vim-minimal-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["vim-filesystem-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["vim-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["vim-X11-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","vim-common-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","vim-debuginfo-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","vim-debugsource-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","vim-enhanced-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","vim-minimal-9.0-41.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-1781.json"}},{"package":{"name":"vim","ecosystem":"ope